# model_table -- the single per-model definition file.
#
# Every per-model *fact* lives here, exactly once. General code (the bridge, the
# client, the boot scripts, detect-model, build_sd) looks its model up in this
# table and never tests a model name itself. Per-model *code* (hardware
# bring-up that can't be a data value) stays in script/lower_half/<model>.sh,
# selected by the model key. So adding a camera is: one row here, plus a
# lower_half script only if its hardware bring-up actually differs.
#
# Columns, whitespace-separated ('#' starts a comment):
#
#   model  sensor  ring_offset  ring_header  high_w  high_h  ptz
#
#   model        model_suffix token: what /backup/init.sh sets and -m carries
#   sensor       MIPI sensor driver basename (e.g. gc3003). detect-model maps a
#                sensor to a model ONLY when exactly one row names it; a sensor
#                shared by several models (gc2053) is ambiguous and ignored.
#   ring_offset  fshare ring control-header size in bytes; 0 = autodetect
#   ring_header  per-frame header bytes before the payload; 0 = autodetect
#   high_w/h     real HIGH-channel (video1) encoder geometry, SPS-verified
#   ptz          yes/no -- real motorized pan/tilt base
#
# A model with no row gets the conservative default (368/28, 2304x1296, no PTZ)
# and a warning; never a silent guess. Keep this list to models we actually
# support -- a row is a claim about real hardware.
y623     gc3003  368  28  2304  1296  no
h52ga    gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  yes
r35gb    gc2053  0    0   1920  1080  yes
y291ga   gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  no
